SUMMARY:Peggy Ratusz and Daddy Longlegs
DESCRIPTION:Bio\nPeggy “Blues Chanteuse” Ratusz\, has won best in Blues awards for the past 17 years as well as best vocalist and most notable local musician who gives back to the community. A three-time semi-finalist in the International Blues Challenge held in Memphis\, TN for the past 36 years\, Ratusz produces her own shows including “Love Letter: A Tribute to Bonnie Raitt\,” and “Blues In the Night” a collection of torchy and tantalizing Jazz standards\, Swing tunes and Blues Shuffles. She’s opened for Tedeschi Trucks band\, Taj Mahal\, Geoff Atchison\, Bob Margolin\, Danielle Nicole Band\, the late Denise LaSalle and the Beach Boys. An advocate for female vocalists and musicians\, she is published each month in SOFIA magazine writing a feature she created; “Women Making Music.” \nWeekend Live Music\nHighland Brewing’s weekend live music series showcases incredible local talent\, regional acts and national touring bands from across the East Coast and beyond. Free and open to all ages (unless noted otherwise)\, it’s the perfect excuse to gather your crew\, listen and vibe to a wide range of genres including soul\, bluegrass\, acoustic\, country\, folk and more.\nLive music typically takes place on our scenic Meadow stage. Shows are rain or shine\, if the weather doesn’t cooperate and we have time to move inside\, the band will play in the Taproom where there’s still plenty of room to boogie.\nChairs\, blankets and well-behaved\, leashed pets are welcome in the Meadow. Please note that coolers and outside alcohol are not permitted on the premises.
URL:https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/peggy-ratusz-and-daddy-longlegs/
LOCATION:Meadow at Highland Brewing Co.\, 12 Old Charlotte Highway\, Suite 200\, Asheville\, NC\, 28803\, United States
CATEGORIES:Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://highlandbrewing.com/wp-content/uploads/Peggy-New.jpg
END:VEVENT
